{
  "format": "golfmap-models-v1",
  "comment": "Every model Omberg can draw (CONTEXT.md 'Model library'): its trees, and since 2026-10-21 the lower vegetation its zone palettes (grass-palette.json) refer to - form grass (vsp:texture:<texture stem>, a VSP texture item), plant or shrub (vsp:<prefab> for the course's own VSP, arborist:<label> for Arborist), no kind, a vsp one sized by its zone items; one asset in several looks is several models (#<variant>). A lower model's look is what every zone item wearing it shows: healthy / dry, material (shader floats), randomDarkening, rootAmbient, alphaCutoff, whitePoint, shadows for VSP; Arborist's own keys (tint, saturation, ...) over plantSettings for Arborist. Change one: bun run models -- look \"Ombergs Golfklubb\" <model> --set healthy=#rrggbb. The migrated Arborist bushes carry no colours: plantSettings' tint decides them, as before. id: arborist:<Arborist catalogue label> or vsp:<Unity prefab>; renderer: what draws it in GSPro. Sizes: a vsp model's from the Unity catalogue, an Arborist model's from data/arborist/catalog-sizes.json (first LOD). The palette refers to these by id. Beech and elm are Arborist-only (Marcus, Arborist Ultra lineup 2026-10-18); the S7 elm's look is his darkened one. Add one: bun run models -- add \"Ombergs Golfklubb\" arborist:<label> --species <species>. Poplars, pines, firs and dwarf pines are Arborist models since 2026-10-20 (their looks moved here from arborist-species.json). billboardAs (a vsp model): the Arborist model drawn as its billboard where the routing makes the tree one (vegetation-rules.json `routing`).",
